WEBVTT

00:00:02.320 --> 00:00:09.000
United States of America and the Prime

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:09.000
Minister of the Kingdom of Thailand.

00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:22.359
>> Thank you very much.

00:00:27.599 --> 00:00:31.920
>> Well, thank you very much. This is a

00:00:29.519 --> 00:00:34.320
great honor. We've been working on this

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:36.480
deal for a long time

00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:39.360
and uh it's going to be a wonderful deal

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:42.800
for both parties I believe. But I'm

00:00:39.360 --> 00:00:45.600
thrilled to join Prime Minister

00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:47.920
Anutton of Thailand as we sign a

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:50.000
historic trade deal between our two

00:00:47.920 --> 00:00:52.239
countries. We do a lot of trade with

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:55.360
Thailand actually.

00:00:52.239 --> 00:00:57.920
It's been a cherished ally of the United

00:00:55.360 --> 00:01:00.239
States for more than 70 years and our

00:00:57.920 --> 00:01:02.559
friendship goes back more than 200 years

00:01:00.239 --> 00:01:05.840
and the prime minister is doing a

00:01:02.559 --> 00:01:08.799
fantastic job. Not an easy one, but he's

00:01:05.840 --> 00:01:10.400
getting it really in shape and he's done

00:01:08.799 --> 00:01:12.080
it's being talked about all over the

00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:12.240
world, the job you're doing. So, thank

00:01:12.080 --> 00:01:14.640
you.

00:01:12.240 --> 00:01:16.640
>> I want to congratulate you.

00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:18.479
>> But he goes back more than 200 years in

00:01:16.640 --> 00:01:22.000
what has always been one of America's

00:01:18.479 --> 00:01:25.520
closest partnerships anywhere in Asia.

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:27.680
Last year at the ASEAN summit, it was my

00:01:25.520 --> 00:01:29.600
honor to work with the prime minister to

00:01:27.680 --> 00:01:34.320
forge peace between Thailand and

00:01:29.600 --> 00:01:36.000
Cambodia. We uh solved a really violent

00:01:34.320 --> 00:01:39.600
situation

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:42.720
and uh I think I did that. I don't think

00:01:39.600 --> 00:01:45.280
I got any credit for it. So, just

00:01:42.720 --> 00:01:48.079
another war that I saved, but I get no

00:01:45.280 --> 00:01:51.280
credit. But that's okay. I don't mind. I

00:01:48.079 --> 00:01:52.880
want to save lives. It's 99.9%.

00:01:51.280 --> 00:01:55.520
But it was it was an honor and you were

00:01:52.880 --> 00:01:58.960
a total professional. Now we're making

00:01:55.520 --> 00:02:00.880
history once again. Today today's deal

00:01:58.960 --> 00:02:02.640
lays the foundation for much stronger

00:02:00.880 --> 00:02:04.880
trading relationship that will bring the

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:06.399
United States and Thailand closer than

00:02:04.880 --> 00:02:08.080
ever before. And I think we are because

00:02:06.399 --> 00:02:10.399
of the relationship that we have. I

00:02:08.080 --> 00:02:11.760
think we probably are the closest we've

00:02:10.399 --> 00:02:15.360
ever been. We're going to do a lot of

00:02:11.760 --> 00:02:18.080
trade. Uh Thailand will eliminate all

00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:19.760
tariffs on US exports, which is

00:02:18.080 --> 00:02:22.080
something that we've been after for a

00:02:19.760 --> 00:02:24.000
long time, and remove substantial

00:02:22.080 --> 00:02:25.920
non-tariff barriers on American

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:28.640
vehicles, medical devices,

00:02:25.920 --> 00:02:30.959
pharmaceuticals, ethanol, and poultry.

00:02:28.640 --> 00:02:33.920
Thailand will also be buying an

00:02:30.959 --> 00:02:36.400
estimated $2.6 billion in additional US

00:02:33.920 --> 00:02:38.560
agricultural products. That makes our

00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:41.280
farmers very happy. We're doing a lot of

00:02:38.560 --> 00:02:43.120
great deals for our farmers. This is an

00:02:41.280 --> 00:02:44.800
incredible victory for both countries,

00:02:43.120 --> 00:02:46.959
both the people of Thailand and the

00:02:44.800 --> 00:02:49.120
American people, and I look forward to

00:02:46.959 --> 00:02:51.599
finalizing the details of our formal

00:02:49.120 --> 00:02:54.319
agreement in the coming weeks. Our staff

00:02:51.599 --> 00:02:56.319
is working on it very diligently, and

00:02:54.319 --> 00:02:59.280
it'll be done, but the concept of what

00:02:56.319 --> 00:03:01.840
we have will be really, very permanent,

00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:03.840
and we're just about there. And we're

00:03:01.840 --> 00:03:06.080
going to actually sign a document right

00:03:03.840 --> 00:03:08.159
now. So, I'd like to invite the prime

00:03:06.080 --> 00:03:11.200
minister say to say a few words and then

00:03:08.159 --> 00:03:13.440
we'll sign a joint statement talking

00:03:11.200 --> 00:03:16.000
about the deal and uh then they're going

00:03:13.440 --> 00:03:17.680
to finalize it and they this is the more

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:20.000
difficult part because it took us a

00:03:17.680 --> 00:03:23.120
while to get to this point. So, Mr.

00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:25.519
Prime Minister, please.

00:03:23.120 --> 00:03:27.040
>> Thank you, Mr. President, Mr.

00:03:25.519 --> 00:03:29.760
Secretaries,

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:32.560
distinguished guests, it is a pleasure

00:03:29.760 --> 00:03:34.640
for me to meet you again and I have to

00:03:32.560 --> 00:03:37.840
thank you for bringing us here to this

00:03:34.640 --> 00:03:40.400
point. I'm pleased that we have reached

00:03:37.840 --> 00:03:42.959
a substantial conclusion in our

00:03:40.400 --> 00:03:45.920
negotiations on the agreement on

00:03:42.959 --> 00:03:48.640
reciprocal trade between the United

00:03:45.920 --> 00:03:51.200
States and Thailand. And I believe the

00:03:48.640 --> 00:03:54.000
agreement will bring greater dynamics to

00:03:51.200 --> 00:03:56.879
our trade relations and open new

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:58.959
opportunities for all stakeholders.

00:03:56.879 --> 00:04:01.519
Mr. President, your leadership in

00:03:58.959 --> 00:04:04.319
bringing this negotiation to a nice

00:04:01.519 --> 00:04:06.879
conclusion like this is greatly greatly

00:04:04.319 --> 00:04:09.200
appreciated and yet there is still a

00:04:06.879 --> 00:04:11.920
little more to do. I'm confident that

00:04:09.200 --> 00:04:15.360
the agreement will be ready for us to

00:04:11.920 --> 00:04:17.440
sign real soon. Thailand attaches great

00:04:15.360 --> 00:04:19.759
importance to its long-standing

00:04:17.440 --> 00:04:22.880
relationship with the United with the

00:04:19.759 --> 00:04:25.199
United States. Our partnership is beyond

00:04:22.880 --> 00:04:26.960
trade and investment. We remain

00:04:25.199 --> 00:04:29.680
committed to strengthening our

00:04:26.960 --> 00:04:32.080
cooperation across areas of mutual

00:04:29.680 --> 00:04:35.040
interest. Today's achievement

00:04:32.080 --> 00:04:37.520
demonstrates what our two countries can

00:04:35.040 --> 00:04:39.759
accomplish by working together. I'm

00:04:37.520 --> 00:04:43.120
confident that it will provide a strong

00:04:39.759 --> 00:04:45.520
foundation for an for an even closer and

00:04:43.120 --> 00:04:47.040
more productive partnership in the years

00:04:45.520 --> 00:04:49.513
ahead. Thank you, Mr. President.

00:04:47.040 --> 00:04:51.533
>> Thank you very much.

00:04:49.513 --> 00:04:51.533
[applause]

00:05:29.120 --> 00:05:36.520
Thank you. Thank you.

00:05:32.240 --> 00:05:36.520
Okay, we will hold that up.

00:05:37.328 --> 00:05:41.160
[applause]

00:05:38.160 --> 00:05:41.160
CONGRATULATIONS.

00:05:41.913 --> 00:05:43.933
[applause]

